      "qc": {
        "base_3x3_1x_and_4x": "All six literal 3x3 repeats saved at native 864x864 and nearest-neighbour 3456x3456. Inspected native complete repeats and 4x 384x384-native viewports containing the entire central tile plus all four adjoining wraps. Additional full-width horizontal and full-height vertical wrap strips inspected at 4x. No continuous perimeter road or inherited 48px street-frame grid; the conspicuous summer city green-band repeat fails separately.",
        "individual_8x": "Inspected every Part E file. Each complete base saved at 8x and inspected through four exact 144x144-native quadrants enlarged to 1152x1152, covering all pixels. Every complete landmark inspected on labelled 8x sheets of four, in both seasons.",
        "standing_landmark_context_1x_and_4x": "All eight towers and all eight stacks sparsely composited onto corresponding tiled district bases in both seasons. Inspected all four complete 576x384 native contexts and both 4x halves of each, covering every sprite and its surroundings. All landmarks remain readable; no placement failure assigned to a sprite because its base has a defect.",
        "alpha_fringe_halo": "All 32 landmarks inspected at 4x over pale, near-black and neutral backgrounds and at 8x over neutral. Alpha values are exactly 0/255; every landmark is one 8-connected opaque component, with zero hidden RGB pixels. No matte fringe, halo, softened edge, backing rectangle or stray opaque island found.",
        "dimensions_placement": "All six bases are 288x288 and opaque. All 32 landmarks are 48x96, horizontally centred with feet ending on row 94 and intact margins. No cropped extremity or wrong-sized canvas. Revised winter towers 3 and 5 now begin at native y=10, matching summer antenna height and position; registered seasonal pairs inspected at 8x.",
        "blur_antialias_noise_muddy_shapes": "Native pixels and limited palettes are intact; no resampling blur or anti-aliasing found. The revised slums remove the previous pervasive roof speckle and retain distinguishable broad metal/tarp patches. Winter industry removes the bright pipe mesh and leaves readable tanks/sheds. City interiors are calmer, but its larger roof silhouettes remain muddy enough to fail both seasons as specified.",
        "lighting_palette": "Top/left landmark planes are lit, right faces shaded. Cream/grey-green metal, dark blue-green ground, cyan and sparse magenta lights fit the approved scifi markers. Seasonal snow uses the cool ramp of the approved winter art at intentionally darker city contrast. No additional wrong-light or palette-clash failure.",
        "duplicates": "Compared complete 8x landmark lineups and seasonal counterparts; no exact raster duplicates among the 38 files. Towers have distinct tiered, globe, wedge, bridge, terrace, observation-deck, split-fin and spiral forms. Stacks have distinct chimney, cooling-tower, gas-holder and refinery configurations. No near-duplicate failure.",
        "winter": "All three winter districts remain populated and recognizable with summer layouts. Broad snow patches vary in coverage and retain exposed surfaces; winters are neither blank nor merely erased. Snow and architecture remain legible on the passed landmarks. Both repaired antennas are restored. The winter city failure is unresolved architectural readability, not the former noisy rim treatment.",
        "peak_lattice_or_range": "Not applicable: Part E contains no peaks or ridges. No Part C file reviewed.",
        "random_8x2_one_cell_tiles": "Not applicable: Part E contains no one-cell terrain tiles. The 48x96 landmarks are standing transparent sprites and were tested in sparse context. Legacy numbered district tiles are outside Part E.",
        "trees_in_forest": "Not applicable: Part E contains no trees or forest floors. No tree/forest verdict issued.",
        "brief_specific_traps": "Stamped cyberpunk grid and repetitive district motifs checked in every base. Egg-crate peaks, Swiss-cheese craters, classical ruins, flat orange autumn and identical crowns apply to files outside Part E and are not grounds to review unrelated files."
      },
