  "fail": [
    {
      "name": "scifi-city-base",
      "problems": "The texture wraps without a continuous street frame, but it still fails the native 3x3 repeat: the wide, flat olive S-shaped green corridor joins into conspicuous horizontal waves, repeated at the same height in every tile. Break that corridor into unequal planted strips/pockets, vary its width and value, and interrupt its cross-tile silhouette with roofs or a paved plaza. The quieter roof interiors are an improvement, but the large forked and U-shaped footprints still have ragged bites, thin protrusions and ambiguous roof/wall junctions in the 4x and 8x views; at 1x several read as grey lumps with lights attached. Redraw those large footprints as deliberate architectural planes with clean parapets and consistent wall depth, and make at least one open plaza visibly distinct from the dark alleys. Keep the restrained neon and seamless ground."
    },
    {
      "name": "scifi-city@winter-base",
      "problems": "Broad roof snow fixes the previous all-over bright-rim noise, but it exposes the unresolved building-shape problem. In the 1x repeated district, the larger branching/H-shaped masses still read as irregular snow-topped lumps; the 4x wrap/context and complete 8x quadrant views show notched, wavering roof silhouettes and roof extensions whose wall planes are unclear. The forked building in the upper-left quarter and the broad branching group in the lower-right quarter are useful repair targets. Rebuild these footprints with deliberate straight or consistently stepped roof edges, connected ledges and a clear roof-to-wall transition, then apply snow within those roof planes. Give the open dark spaces an identifiable paved plaza rather than leaving every gap as undifferentiated alley. Preserve the current broad snow patches, exposed roof areas, anchored layout and dark street contrast; do not restore the noisy white outlines."
    }
  ]
